{
  "slug": "windows-11-no-sound-after-update",
  "title": "Windows 11 No Sound After Update? 7 Ways to Get It Back",
  "description": "Windows 11 has no sound after an update? Run 7 fixes, from the output device to a driver rollback and a Windows update removal.",
  "category": "PC Troubleshooting",
  "tags": [
    "Windows",
    "PC Maintenance",
    "Troubleshooting",
    "Beginner Guide"
  ],
  "url": "https://www.techtips.fun/blog/windows-11-no-sound-after-update/",
  "theme": "github-dark",
  "durationInFrames": 930,
  "scenes": [
    {
      "type": "title",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "title": "Windows 11 No Sound After Update? 7 Ways to Get It Back",
      "subtitle": "Windows 11 has no sound after an update? Run 7 fixes, from the output device to a driver…",
      "durationInFrames": 105
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Before You Start",
      "body": "Save your open work. Test your speakers or headphones on another device. If the sound works on the other device, continue with Fix 1.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 1: Select the Output Device and the Volume",
      "body": "Windows can select the wrong output device after an update. Windows can also set the volume of one app to zero. Open Settings. Select System > Sound.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 2: Run the Audio Troubleshooter",
      "body": "Windows has a troubleshooter that repairs common sound errors. The Get Help app contains the same troubleshooter. Open Settings.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 3: Restart the Audio Services",
      "body": "Every sound on Windows runs through two services: Windows Audio and Windows Audio Endpoint Builder. Without these services, the sound stops.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 4: Turn Off Audio Enhancements and Spatial Sound",
      "body": "Audio enhancements can stop the sound after a driver update. Spatial sound can also block the output. Open Settings. Select System > Sound.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 5: Roll Back the Audio Driver",
      "body": "The update can install a faulty driver. Windows stores the earlier driver on the computer. The rollback restores this driver.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "outro",
      "heading": "Read the full article",
      "body": "New posts every week on the blog.",
      "url": "techtips.fun",
      "durationInFrames": 105
    }
  ],
